{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls6_jpg\\geo\\013.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "a.Igneous Rocks", "conf": 0.882, "box": [[26, 134], [226, 132], [227, 159], [26, 161]]}, {"text": "Igneous rocks are formed as lava cools and hardens. Lava is molten rock material ejected by", "conf": 0.937, "box": [[24, 168], [1145, 180], [1144, 217], [24, 205]]}, {"text": "volcanoes during eruption. Normally igneous rocks are crystalline in nature. Acccrding to the", "conf": 0.934, "box": [[25, 205], [1144, 218], [1143, 248], [25, 235]]}, {"text": "origin, igneous rocks are divided into two types: intrusive and extrusive rocks. Granite, Gabbro,", "conf": 0.936, "box": [[24, 238], [1144, 250], [1143, 283], [24, 271]]}, {"text": "Basaltand Rhyoliteareexamplesof igneousrocks.", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[24, 273], [608, 280], [608, 310], [24, 303]]}, {"text": "Granite", "conf": 0.81, "box": [[125, 568], [204, 568], [204, 596], [125, 596]]}, {"text": "Gabbro", "conf": 0.806, "box": [[425, 574], [500, 574], [500, 599], [425, 599]]}, {"text": "Basalt", "conf": 0.851, "box": [[696, 576], [762, 576], [762, 601], [696, 601]]}, {"text": "Rhyolite", "conf": 0.86, "box": [[969, 574], [1055, 574], [1055, 601], [969, 601]]}, {"text": "b.SedimentaryRocks", "conf": 0.9, "box": [[17, 615], [279, 619], [279, 645], [17, 641]]}, {"text": "Theyaredistinguishedfromotherrocktypesby", "conf": 0.951, "box": [[18, 654], [569, 662], [569, 691], [18, 683]]}, {"text": "their characteristic layer (strata)formation.", "conf": 0.939, "box": [[16, 688], [568, 695], [568, 724], [16, 717]]}, {"text": "That is why theyare also called stratified rocks.", "conf": 0.899, "box": [[17, 721], [567, 727], [567, 757], [17, 750]]}, {"text": "Thematerial that forms sedimentaryrocks are", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[17, 753], [569, 763], [569, 790], [17, 780]]}, {"text": "brought by streams, glaciers and winds. They", "conf": 0.922, "box": [[16, 786], [569, 795], [569, 824], [16, 816]]}, {"text": "often contain fossils of animals,plants and", "conf": 0.918, "box": [[17, 820], [570, 828], [570, 855], [17, 847]]}, {"text": "other organisms.Shale, sandstones, Gypsum,", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[15, 852], [564, 862], [563, 892], [15, 882]]}, {"text": "limestoneand conglomerate areexamples of", "conf": 0.911, "box": [[15, 888], [570, 897], [570, 924], [15, 915]]}, {"text": "sedimentaryrocks.", "conf": 0.913, "box": [[14, 922], [238, 925], [237, 952], [14, 949]]}, {"text": "Sedimentary rocks", "conf": 0.891, "box": [[776, 976], [973, 982], [972, 1009], [776, 1003]]}, {"text": "waz", "conf": 0.603, "box": [[263, 1022], [414, 932], [446, 985], [295, 1075]]}, {"text": "Conglomerate", "conf": 0.885, "box": [[91, 1297], [238, 1300], [237, 1330], [90, 1327]]}, {"text": "Shale", "conf": 0.83, "box": [[540, 1305], [604, 1309], [602, 1337], [538, 1333]]}, {"text": "Sandstone", "conf": 0.875, "box": [[928, 1315], [1040, 1318], [1039, 1345], [927, 1342]]}, {"text": "Gypsum", "conf": 0.766, "box": [[241, 1598], [328, 1598], [328, 1630], [241, 1630]]}, {"text": "Limestone", "conf": 0.853, "box": [[814, 1607], [926, 1611], [925, 1639], [813, 1635]]}, {"text": "Unit 1: Structure of Earth and Types of Rocks", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[4, 1676], [426, 1674], [426, 1704], [4, 1706]]}]}